Run a supported native command against active policy

Usage: shield __internal run [OPTIONS] -- <ARGV>...

Arguments:
  <ARGV>...  Exact absolute executable and literal arguments; no PATH or interpreter lookup

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>
          Owning enrolled project directory [default: .]
      --agent <AGENT>
          Optional agent label, recorded as caller attribution
      --json
          Print one JSON result; commands that change policy refuse JSON mode
      --debug-log-dir <DEBUG_LOG_DIR>
          Write private per-process diagnostics in this directory (also `SHIELD_DEBUG_LOG_DIR`)
      --session-id <SESSION_ID>
          Optional host session ID supplied by the launcher
      --no-debug-log
          Disable diagnostic logging, including automatic debug-build logs
      --tool-use-id <TOOL_USE_ID>
          Optional host tool-call ID
      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Compiled cache location for init, MCP setup or cache preparation
      --cwd <CWD>
          Canonical cwd inside the enrolled project; defaults to its root
      --timeout-ms <TIMEOUT_MS>
          Deadline including preparation; cleanup has a separate short grace period [default: 5000]
      --approval-request <APPROVAL_REQUEST>
          Stored native request selector; only an existing exact operator grant can allow Ask
  -h, --help
          Print help
